ed_for":"Prerequisite for thm-the-two-element-set-is-a-subobject-classifier-for-sets.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-mutual-factorisation-defines-subobject-and-quotient-object-equivalence","used_for":"Prerequisite for the subobject-representation theorem and false statement.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-naturality-of-the-connecting-morphism","used_for":"Prerequisite for thm-naturality-of-the-homology-connecting-morphism.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-noetherian-ring-has-finitely-many-minimal-primes","used_for":"Prerequisite for the height-theorem and parameter-selection lemmas.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-noetherian-ring-quotients-and-localisations","used_for":"Prerequisite for the principal-ideal, height, and polynomial upper-bound items.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-primary-submodule-characterisations","used_for":"Prerequisite for lem-parameter-ideal-equivalent-m-primary.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-prime-spectrum-of-a-localisation-bijection","used_for":"Prerequisite for the principal-ideal reduction, localization, and polynomial-fiber items.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-prime-spectrum-of-a-quotient-bijection","used_for":"Prerequisite for the relative-height, height-theorem, parameter, quotient, and polynomial items.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-quotient-is-domain-iff-ideal-prime","used_for":"Prerequisite for the principal-ideal reduction, polynomial, and affine-dimension-formula items.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-right-adjoints-preserve-limits","used_for":"Prerequisite for thm-the-internal-hom-is-continuous-in-each-variable.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-set-has-all-small-limits","used_for":"Prerequisite for thm-set-is-cartesian-closed.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-snake-lemma-under-the-weaker-stacks-hypotheses","used_for":"Prerequisite for def-preconnecting-arrow-on-cycles.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-the-canonical-mapping-cone-sequence-is-degreewise-split-short-exact","used_for":"Prerequisite for thm-the-cone-long-exact-sequence, fs-a-degreewise-split-short-exact-sequence-of-complexes-has-zero-connecting-map, and ex-a-degreewise-split-sequence-with-nonzero-connecting-map.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-the-kernel-row-and-cokernel-row-of-a-morphism-of-short-exact-sequences-are-exact-at-two-nodes-each","used_for":"Prerequisite for lem-the-cycle-boundary-diagram-associated-to-a-short-exact-sequence-of-complexes.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-transitivity-of-algebraicity","used_for":"Prerequisite for thm-affine-domain-dimension-transcendence-degree.","opened":true}],"concerns":[{"id":"lem-principal-ideal-theorem-associated-prime-step","concern":"Its uncited [F1], “if $x\\in\\mathfrak n$ is not nilpotent and $V(x)=\\{\\mathfrak n\\}$, then $\\dim A=1$,” supplies the substantive dimension bound needed to prove the principal ideal theorem. No declared dependency proves it; establishing its upper bound is already the principal-ideal content used immediately downstream.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"lem-height-theorem-first-generator-reduction","concern":"Step 1.1 asserts that “repeatedly applying the two-step prime-avoidance argument” replaces an arbitrary chain by one with the required $\\mathfrak p_1$ property, but neither [L1]–[L3] nor the proof states that argument or derives the replacement. This is the key construction on which the height-theorem induction depends.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"thm-existence-of-systems-of-parameters","concern":"After [L1] only gives $\\dim(R/(x))\\le d-1$, step 1.2 says induction gives a system of parameters $(\\bar x_2,\\ldots,\\bar x_d)$ of length $d-1$. By the page definition, a system in a quotient of smaller dimension has fewer entries. The proof needs an explicit padding argument (or an exact dimension-drop result).","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"},{"id":"lem-parameter-dimension-drop-is-exact","concern":"[L1] calls the image of $(x_2,\\ldots,x_d)$ a system of parameters in $R/(x)$ before the conclusion $\\dim(R/(x))=d-1$ has been proved. What follows from the original system is maximal radical, not yet the claimed parameter length; the proof only needs that weaker property.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"},{"id":"thm-dimension-formula-for-affine-domains","concern":"The uncited [F1], $\\dim S=\\dim(S_{\\mathfrak q})+\\operatorname{trdeg}_k\\operatorname{Frac}(S/\\mathfrak q)$, becomes exactly the stated affine dimension formula after [L2] and [L3]. Thus the proof assumes its conclusion in an equivalent formulation rather than deriving or citing it.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"def-slice-category-and-the-pullback-functor","concern":"The final sentence says arbitrary chosen pullbacks make $f\\mapsto f^*$ contravariantly functorial. Such choices generally give only canonical natural isomorphisms $(gf)^*\\cong f^*g^*$; strict functoriality requires compatible split-cleavage choices, not merely chosen pullbacks.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"thm-currying-and-uncurrying-are-mutually-inverse","concern":"Step 2.2 invokes a “canonical internal-hom composition isomorphism,” while its cited thm-the-internal-hom-composition-morphism supplies a composition morphism, not the exponential-law isomorphism $(D^C)^B\\cong D^{B\\times C}$. The repeated-currying claim needs a separate adjunction calculation.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"},{"id":"fs-the-left-and-right-internal-homs-agree-in-every-monoidal-category","concern":"Its [A1] reverses the handedness for $R$-bimodules: under the page convention $[X,-]$ is right adjoint to $-\\otimes_R X$, so it is built from left $R$-linear maps $\\operatorname{Hom}_{R-}(X,-)$, not $\\operatorname{Hom}_{-R}(X,-)$. The two annihilator computations are thereby assigned to the wrong named internal homs.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"def-preconnecting-arrow-on-cycles","concern":"The definition is stated for complexes in an arbitrary abelian category but defines $\\widetilde\\partial_n$ by elements $z\\in Z_n(C)$, lifts $b$, and expressions $b+i_n(u)$. Those element-level operations do not define a morphism in a general abelian category as written; the cited snake construction could provide one, but the item does not formulate that construction as its definition.","severity":"would-be-fatal"}],"alerts":[],"seams_checked":[]}